  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A source of constant voltage <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is connected to a resistance<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and two ideal inductors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> through a switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> as shown. There is no mutual inductance between the two inductors. The switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is initially open. At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> , the switch is closed and current begins to flow. Which of the following options is/are correct?<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0012_0ec8936fbdaa.png\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The ratio of the currents through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is fixed at all times <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "After a long time, the current through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> will be <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "After a long time, the current through <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> will be <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
